{
 "description": "Every box and result row declared in a pound unit that the metric-convention pass (GH-IMP-013, GH-DEF-025) classified, on the Imperial page of the 696 calculators. cls = force: a calculated or specified FORCE, declared lb / lbf, newtons in Metric. cls = converter: a converter's own result row, named for its own unit, identical in both systems. cls = mass-rated: a vehicle / trailer / component weight or a manufacturer rating that is stated as a MASS (GVWR, GCWR, payload, tongue weight, hitch, winch and recovery-point ratings), declared lbs, kilograms in Metric. cls = load: a load-transfer result, corner / axle load or per-tire vertical load: a force by physics, but the number a corner-weight scale or a tire load index gives, so it is read and shown as the MASS-EQUIVALENT scale reading, declared lbs, kilograms in Metric (owner decisions D1 and D2 in GH-IMP-013, approved 2026-10-13; 11 outputs and 5 per-tire inputs). The forces that follow from such a load (available tire force, rolling-resistance force, contact-patch pressure) stay newtons or bar. premium/tests/mass-force.test.js fails if a row declared lb / lbf appears that is not listed, if a listed force / converter row stops being one, or if a mass-rated or load row is not declared lbs. The unit field of a row is the unit it was declared in when it was classified (before the conversions of GH-IMP-013). The 11 rows of materials and thermal masses fixed earlier (GH-DEF-006) are listed in MASS_ROWS in that test. Generated by scanning every calculator in Imperial at default state; the pound-force rows were classified from the formulas and from manufacturer / industry practice, not from the label text.",
